WEBVTT

1
00:00:15.179 --> 00:00:17.822
Help! A drowning woman!"

2
00:00:18.382 --> 00:00:19.043
Jack yelled.

3
00:00:19.683 --> 00:00:21.385
He didn't know whether anyone heard him.

4
00:00:22.326 --> 00:00:26.069
It was so early in the morning, only a few minutes past six o'clock.

5
00:00:26.870 --> 00:00:29.232
Nobody seemed to be awake or outside.

6
00:00:30.188 --> 00:00:31.449
He'd have to rescue Mrs.

7
00:00:31.509 --> 00:00:34.330
Wilson himself—or try to, anyway.

8
00:00:35.230 --> 00:00:39.872
Luckily, he'd learned a little about first aid and CPR from taking a class at his pool in

9
00:00:39.912 --> 00:00:44.994
Oklahoma. He dived under the water and swam toward her as fast as he could.

10
00:00:49.176 --> 00:00:53.298
But when he got closer to her still body, he wasn't sure what to do.

11
00:00:54.058 --> 00:00:55.719
Mrs. Wilson was so large.

12
00:00:56.079 --> 00:00:57.660
How could he possibly lift her?

13
00:00:58.988 --> 00:01:01.249
The only thing Jack could do was try.

14
00:01:01.930 --> 00:01:05.011
He reached the bottom of the pool and managed to lift Mrs.

15
00:01:05.051 --> 00:01:06.032
Wilson a little bit.

16
00:01:07.573 --> 00:01:09.274
He wrapped one arm around her neck.

17
00:01:10.334 --> 00:01:15.878
Using his other hand, he paddled up through the water, kicking with all his strength to the top.

18
00:01:19.380 --> 00:01:26.383
At the surface his lungs gasped for air, choking and heaving, the strange noises he made scaring him.

19
00:01:29.368 --> 00:01:32.271
But what scared him a hundred times more was Mrs.

20
00:01:32.331 --> 00:01:34.212
Wilson's complete stillness.

21
00:01:35.153 --> 00:01:37.955
Jack wondered how long she'd lain at the bottom of the pool.

22
00:01:39.056 --> 00:01:40.137
Could she ever recover?

23
00:01:40.497 --> 00:01:41.478
Was she already dead?

24
00:01:41.839 --> 00:01:42.919
This was terrifying!

25
00:01:44.561 --> 00:01:48.784
Jack forced the scary thoughts from his mind so he could focus on getting Mrs.

26
00:01:48.824 --> 00:01:50.145
Wilson out of the water.

27
00:01:51.086 --> 00:01:55.010
He had to get her to the edge of the pool and then somehow lift her large body

28
00:01:55.190 --> 00:01:55.870
up to the deck.

29
00:01:56.751 --> 00:01:58.813
With his left arm, Jack held Mrs.

30
00:01:58.853 --> 00:02:00.453
Wilson's head above the surface.

31
00:02:02.014 --> 00:02:04.656
Then he began kicking and paddling furiously.

32
00:02:07.557 --> 00:02:12.040
Once they reached the side of the pool, Jack tried to summon the energy to lift Mrs.

33
00:02:12.080 --> 00:02:12.720
Wilson out.

34
00:02:14.241 --> 00:02:19.224
Just then he spotted a man in a business suit walking out of his apartment about twenty yards

35
00:02:19.284 --> 00:02:25.327
away. Jack had never been so happy to see another human being.

36
00:02:25.347 --> 00:02:30.946
"Help!" Jack tried to shout, but by now, he could barely speak.

37
00:02:31.687 --> 00:02:33.028
He took a hand off Mrs.

38
00:02:33.088 --> 00:02:36.150
Wilson for a few seconds to wave it frantically in the air.

39
00:02:37.091 --> 00:02:39.412
The businessman spotted him and ran over.

40
00:02:41.353 --> 00:02:44.556
He bent down by the edge of the pool and put his hands under Mrs.

41
00:02:44.596 --> 00:02:45.516
Wilson's shoulders.

42
00:02:46.897 --> 00:02:50.680
As Jack pushed her body forward, the man dragged her out.

43
00:02:52.281 --> 00:02:53.642
Jack jumped out of the pool.

44
00:02:53.662 --> 00:02:55.943
"She's not breathing!"

45
00:02:56.324 --> 00:02:56.784
he cried.

46
00:02:57.408 --> 00:02:58.889
He helped the man lay Mrs.

47
00:02:58.949 --> 00:02:59.889
Wilson on her back.

48
00:03:01.230 --> 00:03:05.211
The man grabbed a cell phone from his jacket pocket and called 911.

49
00:03:06.312 --> 00:03:09.533
Meanwhile, Jack shouted for help and pounded on Mrs.

50
00:03:09.573 --> 00:03:15.596
Wilson's chest, trying to imitate the CPR motions he'd seen in his first aid class back in Oklahoma.

51
00:03:18.157 --> 00:03:19.458
Two young women ran over.

52
00:03:21.999 --> 00:03:24.000
One woman said, "I'm in nursing school.

53
00:03:24.160 --> 00:03:24.880
I know CPR."

54
00:03:25.812 --> 00:03:30.474
Jack gratefully moved out of her way and dropped down on the deck, exhausted.

55
00:03:32.295 --> 00:03:34.916
The nursing student pressed her hands against Mrs.

56
00:03:34.976 --> 00:03:37.817
Wilson's chest, working hard and fast.

57
00:03:40.698 --> 00:03:41.158
But Mrs.

58
00:03:41.198 --> 00:03:42.659
Wilson lay still.

59
00:03:43.359 --> 00:03:45.860
By now a few more people were standing nearby.

60
00:03:45.880 --> 00:03:48.161
"Where are the paramedics?"

61
00:03:48.601 --> 00:03:49.642
murmured the businessman.

62
00:03:49.662 --> 00:03:51.162
"They're taking forever!"

63
00:03:52.343 --> 00:03:54.204
The nursing student had tilted Mrs.

64
00:03:54.244 --> 00:03:55.124
Wilson's head back.

65
00:03:56.412 --> 00:03:58.153
Next she pinched Mrs.

66
00:03:58.193 --> 00:04:00.535
Wilson's nose and breathed into her mouth.

67
00:04:03.978 --> 00:04:04.658
Still nothing.

68
00:04:04.678 --> 00:04:09.362
"This is awful," Jack thought, watching the woman work.

69
00:04:09.942 --> 00:04:10.583
"What if Mrs.

70
00:04:10.643 --> 00:04:11.563
Wilson dies?"

71
00:04:12.424 --> 00:04:14.626
By now his parents were probably awake.

72
00:04:15.286 --> 00:04:17.648
Maybe one of them would come to the pool to check on him.

73
00:04:18.588 --> 00:04:23.112
A siren finally sounded in the distance, growing louder as it approached.

74
00:04:27.724 --> 00:04:29.065
The woman pressed on Mrs.

75
00:04:29.125 --> 00:04:30.226
Wilson's chest again.

76
00:04:31.446 --> 00:04:33.387
Suddenly water gushed from Mrs.

77
00:04:33.427 --> 00:04:34.188
Wilson's mouth.

78
00:04:36.309 --> 00:04:37.410
She sputtered for air.

79
00:04:38.030 --> 00:04:39.371
Then she was breathing!

80
00:04:42.993 --> 00:04:44.113
The crowd cheered.

81
00:04:47.355 --> 00:04:50.037
Jack let out a long, deep, thankful breath.

82
00:04:52.898 --> 00:04:54.559
The nursing student helped Mrs.

83
00:04:54.599 --> 00:04:55.420
Wilson to sit up.

84
00:04:56.500 --> 00:04:59.481
Mrs. Wilson wiped her mouth and looked confused.

85
00:05:00.982 --> 00:05:02.683
The ambulance parked near the pool.

86
00:05:02.703 --> 00:05:06.604
"Give us room!"

87
00:05:06.964 --> 00:05:07.905
a paramedic shouted.

88
00:05:09.205 --> 00:05:11.286
She and another paramedic ran toward Mrs.

89
00:05:11.326 --> 00:05:15.308
Wilson. "Are you okay?"

90
00:05:15.728 --> 00:05:16.668
Jack asked Mrs.

91
00:05:16.708 --> 00:05:19.370
Wilson. The older woman looked at him.

92
00:05:20.050 --> 00:05:23.251
"What a dumb question, Jack," she muttered.

93
00:05:23.871 --> 00:05:27.337
Her voice was weak, but she almost sounded like her usual self.

94
00:05:28.677 --> 00:05:30.038
"I almost drowned.

95
00:05:30.718 --> 00:05:32.738
Of course I'm not okay."

96
00:05:32.758 --> 00:05:36.920
"I found you unconscious on the bottom of the pool," Jack said.

97
00:05:36.940 --> 00:05:41.941
"This boy got you to the side of the pool on his own," the businessman said.

98
00:05:42.782 --> 00:05:44.342
He pointed to the nursing student.

99
00:05:44.362 --> 00:05:46.383
"She gave you CPR."

100
00:05:48.143 --> 00:05:49.404
Mrs. Wilson scowled.

101
00:05:49.424 --> 00:05:55.797
"Maybe if Jack were a better swimmer, he would have reached me quicker and I wouldn't have needed

102
00:05:55.937 --> 00:06:01.879
CPR. And the girl who did the CPR pushed too hard on my chest.

103
00:06:02.579 --> 00:06:04.560
I'm sure she gave me bruises.

104
00:06:05.880 --> 00:06:08.981
And furthermore, these paramedics are worthless.

105
00:06:09.081 --> 00:06:12.042
I've had pizza arrive faster than they did!"

106
00:06:13.482 --> 00:06:14.303
Jack grinned.

107
00:06:15.103 --> 00:06:18.964
Mrs. Wilson was definitely back to her old cranky self.

108
00:06:19.884 --> 00:06:23.206
"We're going to take you to the hospital, one of the paramedics said to Mrs.

109
00:06:23.246 --> 00:06:25.307
Wilson. "You need to be checked out."

110
00:06:26.148 --> 00:06:26.808
They put Mrs.

111
00:06:26.848 --> 00:06:27.889
Wilson on a stretcher.

112
00:06:27.909 --> 00:06:32.451
"Did you stop for breakfast on the way over here?"

113
00:06:32.951 --> 00:06:34.972
Mrs. Wilson asked sarcastically.

114
00:06:36.773 --> 00:06:40.035
The paramedics just smiled and carried her to the ambulance.

115
00:06:43.017 --> 00:06:46.059
After they left, the businessman shook Jack's hand.

116
00:06:46.079 --> 00:06:48.220
"Good job."

117
00:06:49.112 --> 00:06:52.913
"The world needs more young people like you," an older woman chimed in.

118
00:06:52.933 --> 00:06:55.774
"That was a very impressive rescue."

119
00:06:57.174 --> 00:06:57.855
Jack laughed.

120
00:06:59.535 --> 00:07:00.435
"I'm not sure Mrs.

121
00:07:00.515 --> 00:07:02.176
Wilson was very impressed by me!

122
00:07:02.676 --> 00:07:04.017
But I'm glad she's okay."

123
00:07:05.097 --> 00:07:08.538
Looking around, he realized that quite a crowd had gathered.

124
00:07:09.458 --> 00:07:14.940
The people from his apartment building were of all ages and many races, but the faces looked the

125
00:07:14.980 --> 00:07:19.169
same. They all wore identical expressions of relief.

126
00:07:20.889 --> 00:07:24.570
Jack's mother burst through the crowd and threw her arms around her son.

127
00:07:26.311 --> 00:07:28.411
"Jack! We heard you rescued Mrs.

128
00:07:28.451 --> 00:07:30.332
Wilson. You're a hero!"

129
00:07:31.452 --> 00:07:35.633
His father stood behind them, holding Luke, who was still in his pajamas.

130
00:07:35.653 --> 00:07:37.854
"I'm very proud of you, son."

131
00:07:37.874 --> 00:07:39.574
"Me too.

132
00:07:39.714 --> 00:07:40.955
You're like Superman!"

133
00:07:41.375 --> 00:07:41.895
Luke said.

134
00:07:41.915 --> 00:07:45.776
"Things can't get any better than this," Jack thought.

135
00:07:46.860 --> 00:07:48.322
But then they did.

136
00:07:48.922 --> 00:07:50.044
Laura rushed over.

137
00:07:50.064 --> 00:07:53.788
"You're so brave, Jack!

138
00:07:54.088 --> 00:07:55.730
That was an amazing rescue!"

139
00:07:55.750 --> 00:07:58.713
"It was nothing," Jack said.

140
00:07:59.253 --> 00:08:01.055
He winced as his voice cracked.

141
00:08:02.157 --> 00:08:08.343
And then things got even better: Laura leaned forward and kissed him on the cheek.
